    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All required files have been successfully created in the current working directory. The files include:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_labels.py - detects labels or objects in a static image using AWS Rekognition.\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] describe_image.py - generates a short visual description for an image using AWS Rekognition.\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] detect_image_text.py - detects text appearing inside an image using AWS Textract.\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] score_image_safety.py - checks an image for unsafe or policy-sensitive visual content using AWS Rekognition.\n5. [HELPER] vision_client.py - provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Static Image and Visual Understanding.\n6. [HELPER] vision_models.py - defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Static Image and Visual Understanding.\n7. [LATER-STEP] image_summary.py - summarizes visual analysis results using AWS Rekognition and vision_models.\n8. [LATER-STEP] alt_text_translate.py - translates generated image descriptions using AWS Translate.\n9. [LATER-STEP] visual_safety_text.py - checks generated visual labels for unsafe text using AWS Comprehend.\n10. [LATER-STEP] image_asset_archive.py - archives image-analysis artifacts and derived captions in managed object storage using AWS S3.",
